{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_11\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_7e30e869d7c995fa\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_7e30e869d7c995fa/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Korean language QA edge cases\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_fd22fa33e77a761978a1a44e\", \"member_010c2785d8ee301e24894be8\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that one paragraph uses polite Korean and the next uses casual Korean, and asks which QA rule to follow.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports in the register thread that casual speech was not requested and asks for the two Korean sentences so a language reviewer can inspect the endings.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks for the precise Korean endings for language QA in the register thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructs that Korean QA needs context and sentence endings before severity is decided in the register thread, and says the prior-batch discussion is not yet verified. Verbatim quote: \\\"Before deciding severity, Korean QA needs the context and the sentence endings; the prior-batch discussion is not yet verified.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks QA to clarify a case in which the prompt is Korean but the answer includes an English paragraph in the middle.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks in the language-change thread whether the case involves a single borrowed term or a substantial unrequested language change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ directs Korean register cases to appropriate Korean language QA with exact endings and surrounding context, requires checking quotations and addressee changes, and says the grade depends on demonstrated impact rather than the shift alone.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ accepts ordinary loanwords, requires assessment against context and the required output language, and distinguishes an unrequested full paragraph in another language from a single English word.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current content-quality rubric requires language QA to establish context and impact for disputed locale-specific cases; a major language-adherence defect requires a substantial unrequested mismatch violating the requirement, and a major register defect requires materially disruptive inconsistency confirmed in context.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:db772378\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current specialist-routing instructions require selecting expertise for the language being evaluated and seeking clarification rather than inventing a required locale.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:9199a335\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier batch-10 referral records routing a Korean register case involving a quoted casual sentence for Korean expert review with endings and surrounding context; its recorded outcome is pending expert review, and its scope is that case rather than a standing exemption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multi-korean-referral@1.0:929d7cee\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided threads contain no final scoring decision: the register thread ends with the team lead's request for context before severity is decided, and the language-change thread ends with a QA tutor's clarifying question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors ask about different Korean QA cases: a shift between polite and casual speech, and an English paragraph within an answer to a Korean prompt.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Neither thread establishes a final scoring decision; the register case has a team lead instruction to obtain context before deciding severity.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the register thread, a tutor and a QA tutor requested the Korean sentences or precise endings for language review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the language-change thread, a QA tutor asked whether the English was a borrowed term or a substantial unrequested language change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ directs Korean register cases to appropriate language QA and says an ending change alone does not justify a major penalty.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current language-adherence guidance distinguishes ordinary loanwords from an unrequested full paragraph in another language.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier batch-10 referral records a Korean register case routed for expert review, with its outcome still pending in that record; it is not a standing rule for these cases.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multi-korean-referral@1.0:929d7cee\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Ask a language specialist to review. Instruction: Refer both cases to Korean language QA for case-specific assessment, keeping the register and language-adherence questions separate. Draft to copy: For Korean language QA review:\\n- A tutor reports polite Korean in one paragraph and casual Korean in the next. Please provide the exact sentence endings and surrounding context, including quotations and any speaker or addressee changes.\\n- A tutor reports an English paragraph within an answer to a Korean prompt. Please provide the prompt and answer so QA can check the output-language requirement and the extent of the change.\\nPlease assess register and language adherence separately, using demonstrated impact. A register shift alone does not justify a major penalty; ordinary loanwords are not automatically language-adherence errors. Scope: This referral requests assessment, not a predetermined grade; the register case remains subject to the team lead's thread-specific requirement for context before severity is decided.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:db772378\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:9199a335\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: Current guidance calls for language-matched expertise and context-based scoring. A focused referral follows that guidance without turning either reported symptom into an automatic major penalty.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:db772378\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:9199a335\", \"k:multi-korean-referral@1.0:929d7cee\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): The language-change scoring question remains unanswered after a QA tutor's clarifying question, making Korean QA review appropriate alongside the register case awaiting context.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_fd22fa33e77a761978a1a44e\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_fd22fa33e77a761978a1a44e is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The tutor's scoring question is not finally answered, but the team lead establishes the next step: obtain context and sentence endings for Korean QA before deciding severity.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897232.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_010c2785d8ee301e24894be8\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_010c2785d8ee301e24894be8 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor requests clarification, and the QA tutor responds with a question about the extent of the language change rather than a scoring answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: The two tutors describe distinct, contained QA edge cases with applicable guidance and requests for case details. The messages do not establish conflicting scoring decisions, inability to work, or broader disruption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932114.000145\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897137.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897193.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790932171.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:recurrence\", \"kind\": \"HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Retrieved records show this problem occurred before.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multi-korean-referral@1.0:929d7cee\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U004\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U004 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790897091.000160\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"report